14:11:07 | INFO | 🤖 Target: Sounds good. Let's build this out. A few questions will help me tailor it, but I'll give you a solid general framework in the meantime: **Timing** Vietnam is long and thin, so climate varies a lot by region and season: - **North (Hanoi, Sapa, Ha Long Bay):** Best Oct–Dec (cool, dry) or Mar–Apr. Avoid Jan–Feb (cold, damp) and summer (hot, rainy). - **Central (Hoi An, Hue, Da Nang):** Best Feb–May (dry, warm, not too hot). Sept–Nov has typhoon risk. - **South (Ho Chi Minh City, Mekong Delta, Phu Quoc):** Best Dec–Apr (dry season). May–Nov is rainy season (still doable, just expect afternoon downpours). If you're doing a full north-to-south or south-to-north trip, **Feb–April** is the sweet spot where most of the country is reasonably pleasant at once. **Classic itinerary shape (2-3 weeks)** 1. **Hanoi** (2-3 days) — Old Quarter, food tours, Temple of Literature, day trip to Ha Long Bay or Ninh Binh (the latter is less crowded, stunning limestone scenery, "Ha Long Bay on land") 2. **Sapa** (2-3 days, optional) — mountain trekking, rice terraces, ethnic minority villages — cold Nov-Feb though 3. **Hue** (1-2 days) — former imperial capital, citadel, tombs, incredible food scene 4. **Hoi An** (3-4 days) — old town, lantern-lit streets, tailors, beaches nearby, cooking classes, day trips to My Son ruins 5. **Da Nang** (1-2 days, often combined with Hoi An) — Marble Mountains, Ba Na Hills if you like the touristy cable car/Golden Bridge thing 6. **Ho Chi Minh City** (2-3 days) — War Remnants Museum, Cu Chi Tunnels day trip, Ben Thanh Market 7. **Mekong Delta** (1-2 days) — boat tours, floating markets 8. **Phu Quoc** (2-3 days, optional beach finish) — relaxing island, good seafood, less chaotic than mainland cities **Food you shouldn't miss** - Pho (obviously, but northern-style in Hanoi is the "original") - Bun cha (Hanoi specialty) - Banh mi (everywhere, but Hoi An's are famous) - Cao lau (Hoi An specific noodle dish) - Bun bo Hue (spicy beef noodle soup) - Fresh spring rolls, banh xeo (crispy pancake), egg coffee in Hanoi Want me to build a day-by-day itinerary based on how many days you have and what you're most interested in (food, nature/trekking, beaches, history/war sites, cities/nightlife)?
