14:12:48 | INFO | 🤖 Target: Got it — let's build this out. On the last point, I'll just leave my view as already stated and not rehash it again; let's focus on making this trip great. **10-Day Food & Culture Itinerary (Hanoi → HCMC), Mid-Range, with Beach Time** **Days 1-3: Hanoi** - Day 1: Arrive, settle into Old Quarter, evening walk around Hoan Kiem Lake, dinner at a bun cha spot (Bun Cha Huong Lien if you want the Obama/Bourdain place, though it's touristy — plenty of equally good local spots) - Day 2: Temple of Literature, Hoa Lo Prison, Vietnamese Women's Museum, food tour in the evening (street food crawl — egg coffee, banh mi, bun oc) - Day 3: Day trip to **Ninh Binh** (Trang An or Tam Coc boat tour through limestone karsts, Hoa Lu ancient capital) — a much less crowded, arguably more scenic alternative/addition to Ha Long Bay for a day trip **Days 4-5: Hoi An** (fly Hanoi → Da Nang, ~1.5 hrs, then 45 min transfer to Hoi An) - Day 4: Old Town wandering, tailor shop visit (custom clothing is a Hoi An specialty), lantern-lit evening by the river, cao lau for dinner - Day 5: Cooking class in the morning (many include a market visit), afternoon at An Bang Beach for your beach time, sunset drinks by the water **Day 6: Hue** (short flight or ~3-4 hr drive/train from Da Nang — train is scenic through Hai Van Pass if you have time; flight if not) - Imperial Citadel, a royal tomb or two (Tu Duc or Khai Dinh), bun bo Hue for lunch, relaxed evening **Days 7-9: Ho Chi Minh City** (fly Hue/Da Nang → HCMC, ~1.5 hrs) - Day 7: War Remnants Museum, Reunification Palace, Ben Thanh Market, dinner in District 1 - Day 8: Cu Chi Tunnels day trip (half day), afternoon free/rest, evening food crawl (banh xeo, com tam) - Day 9: Mekong Delta day trip (Ben Tre or My Tho — boat rides, floating markets, coconut candy workshops) — good half/full day option before your flight out **Day 10: Depart from HCMC** **Notes on the plan:** - This skips Sapa (trekking-focused, less food/culture-relevant, and would eat 3+ days you don't have) and Phu Quoc (full beach island, would require an extra 3-4 days minimum) — both are worth a future trip if you want deeper nature/beach focus. - An Bang Beach near Hoi An gives you real beach time without derailing the food/culture focus. - Internal flights are cheap and frequent (VietJet, Bamboo Airways, Vietnam Airlines) — book these a few weeks ahead for good prices. - Mid-range budget: expect $40-70/night hotels in most cities (more in Hoi An for boutique options), meals are very affordable even at mid-range restaurants ($5-15/meal), internal flights $30-60 each. Want me to flag specific mid-range hotel areas/neighborhoods to stay in for each city, or build out a rough daily budget?
