14:14:03 | INFO | 🤖 Target: Here's a mid-range daily budget breakdown, per person, in USD: **Accommodation** (mid-range, private hotel room) - Hanoi: $35-45/night x 3 = $105-135 - Hoi An: $40-55/night x 2 = $80-110 - Hue: $30-40/night x 1 = $30-40 - HCMC: $35-50/night x 3 = $105-150 - **Subtotal: ~$320-435** **Food** (mid-range: mix of street food + sit-down restaurants) - Breakfast: often included at hotel, or $2-4 if not - Lunch: $4-8 (local spots) to $10-15 (nicer sit-down) - Dinner: $8-15 (local/mid-range restaurant), $15-25 if you splurge occasionally - Daily average: **$20-35/day x 10 = $200-350** - (Street food specifically is often $1-3 a dish — you can eat extremely well on the lower end of this range) **Internal transport** - Hanoi → Da Nang flight: $30-50 - Da Nang/Hoi An → Hue (train or car transfer): $10-25 - Hue → HCMC flight: $35-55 - Local transport (Grab, taxis, motorbike taxis) throughout: ~$5-10/day x 10 = $50-100 - **Subtotal: ~$130-230** **Activities/Tours** - Ninh Binh day trip (boat tour, entrance fees): $25-40 - Hoi An cooking class: $25-35 - Cu Chi Tunnels tour: $15-25 - Mekong Delta day trip: $20-35 - Museum/site entrance fees (Citadel, Reunification Palace, War Remnants Museum, etc.): $5-10 each, ~$30-40 total - Tailor-made clothing in Hoi An (optional, highly variable): $30-100+ per item - **Subtotal: ~$150-250** (excluding tailoring) **Miscellaneous** (SIM card, tips, incidentals, souvenirs, bottled water, coffee) - **~$50-80 for the trip** --- **Total estimate for 10 days: ~$850-1,350 per person**, excluding international flights to/from Vietnam. This assumes: - Two people splitting hotel rooms (cuts accommodation roughly in half per person if traveling as a pair) - Mid-range comfort, not luxury, not backpacker-bare-bones - A few splurges built in (better dinners, one or two nicer tours) **Ways to flex the budget:** - Going leaner on food (more street food, less sit-down) can easily save $10-15/day - Skipping one internal flight (e.g., train instead of flying Hue-adjacent legs) saves some cost but adds travel time - Tailoring in Hoi An is the biggest variable — easy to spend $200+ if you get multiple garments made, or skip it entirely and save that chunk Want me to also map out a day-by-day cash flow (how much to carry vs. card use) or best practices for currency exchange and ATM withdrawals while there?
