14:15:39 | INFO | 🤖 Target: Here's a rough daily pacing schedule for the full 10 days. Times are flexible guides, not rigid — Vietnam rewards a bit of spontaneity, especially around food stops. --- **Day 1 — Arrive Hanoi** - Morning/early afternoon: Arrive, transfer to hotel, check in, rest/shower after flight - 4:00 PM: Walk around Hoan Kiem Lake, get oriented in the Old Quarter - 6:30 PM: Dinner — bun cha or a street food stall - Evening: Early night to adjust to time zone **Day 2 — Hanoi** - 8:00 AM: Breakfast, then Temple of Literature - 10:00 AM: Hoa Lo Prison - 12:00 PM: Lunch (try bun rieu or pho) - 2:00 PM: Vietnamese Women's Museum or free wander/shopping in Old Quarter - 5:30 PM: Evening street food crawl — egg coffee, banh mi, nem - Optional: water puppet show (short, touristy but fun, ~45 min) **Day 3 — Ninh Binh Day Trip** - 6:30 AM: Early departure (2-hour drive) - 8:30 AM: Trang An or Tam Coc boat tour (2-3 hrs) - 12:00 PM: Lunch near Ninh Binh - 1:30 PM: Hoa Lu ancient capital or bike ride through rice paddies - 4:00 PM: Head back to Hanoi - 7:00 PM: Arrive Hanoi, relaxed dinner, early night (long day) **Day 4 — Fly to Da Nang, transfer to Hoi An** - Morning: Flight to Da Nang (~1.5 hrs), transfer to Hoi An (~45 min) - Afternoon: Check in, wander Old Town, browse tailor shops - Evening: Lantern-lit riverside walk, dinner (try cao lau) **Day 5 — Hoi An + Beach** - 8:30 AM: Cooking class (often includes market visit, runs 3-4 hrs) - 1:00 PM: Lunch (part of the cooking class usually) - 3:00 PM: Head to An Bang Beach, relax for the afternoon - 6:30 PM: Sunset drinks by the beach - 8:00 PM: Dinner back in Hoi An or beachside **Day 6 — Hue** - Morning: Transfer to Hue (train via Hai Van Pass ~2.5-3 hrs if scenic route, or short flight) - Early afternoon: Check in, lunch (bun bo Hue) - 2:30 PM: Imperial Citadel - 4:30 PM: One royal tomb (Tu Duc or Khai Dinh) - Evening: Relaxed dinner by the Perfume River **Day 7 — Fly to HCMC** - Morning: Flight to HCMC (~1.5 hrs) - Early afternoon: Check in, orient in District 1 - 2:30 PM: Reunification Palace - 4:00 PM: War Remnants Museum (allow 1.5-2 hrs, it's heavy but essential) - Evening: Dinner in District 1, early night if tired from travel day **Day 8 — Cu Chi Tunnels + HCMC** - 7:00 AM: Depart for Cu Chi Tunnels (half-day tour, ~4-5 hrs round trip incl. site time) - 12:30 PM: Back in HCMC, lunch - Afternoon: Rest, or Ben Thanh Market for souvenirs - Evening: Food crawl — banh xeo, com tam, rooftop bar for a skyline view **Day 9 — Mekong Delta Day Trip** - 7:00 AM: Depart for Ben Tre or My Tho - Morning: Boat tour through canals, floating markets, coconut candy workshop - 12:30 PM: Lunch on the water or riverside - Afternoon: Return to HCMC by mid-late afternoon - Evening: Final dinner — treat yourself to a nicer restaurant to close out the trip **Day 10 — Depart** - Morning: Last-minute shopping/breakfast - Airport transfer based on flight time --- **Pacing notes:** - Days 3, 8, and 9 are your long/early days (day trips) — plan lighter evenings after those. - Build in 15-20 min buffer between activities in HCMC and Hanoi for traffic. - Meals are intentionally loose-timed — Vietnamese food culture is casual about exact meal times, so let hunger and street food smells guide you as much as the schedule. - If Day 6 (Hue) feels rushed with only a partial day, consider trimming a half-day off HCMC (Day 8) and adding it to Hue instead — flexible either way. Want me to also flag which specific restaurants/stalls are worth seeking out in each city, or is the plan solid enough to run with as-is?
